  "title": {
    "text": "Regions that aged faster tended to see bigger falls in job churn",
    "subtitle": [
      "ITL2 regions: rise in median age against the % change in the job reallocation rate, 2003\u201307 to 2020\u201324 (correlation -0.52; -0.45 excl. London).",
      "Slow-ageing city regions saw the smallest falls; fast-ageing rural regions some of the largest. Northern Ireland excluded (no reliable data before 2011).",
      "Sources: ONS Longitudinal Business Database (Secure Access, SN 9501); ONS, NRS and NISRA population estimates; authors' calculations."
    ]
  },
